              "yearFrom": 1401,
              "yearTo": 1500,
              "sentence": {
                "id": "s4.b1.1",
                "text": "15th-century resist-printed fragments from Gujarat were found at Fustat in Egypt.",
                "level": "PROVISIONAL",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "id": "a8fba274-8398-5e67-84fc-7af01f82c336",
                    "claimId": "c11f4137-eabe-5a86-91f5-a2a42aba85f2",
                    "sourceId": "f60ab91b-7057-56fe-a4c0-17664472b776",
                    "quote": "Early evidence of Gujarat's involvement in international trade of colourful block printed textiles comes from the fragments found at the Fostat excavations in Egypt. These have been dated back to the fifteenth century and have been printed by the resist printing technique.",
                    "locator": "§ \"Abstract\"",
                    "context": null,
                    "evidence": "QUOTED",
                    "level": "PROVISIONAL"
                  }
                ],
                "translated": false,
                "terms": []
              }
            },
            {
              "place": 1,
              "yearFrom": 1586,
              "yearTo": 1586,
              "sentence": {
                "id": "s4.b1.2",
                "text": "A legend links the craft to Dhamadka following a 16th-century migration.",
                "level": "PROVISIONAL",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "id": "e3248188-5709-5f16-a717-25796fedea4a",
                    "claimId": "77b4e851-c1cd-5561-81a9-018e6e5086a6",
                    "sourceId": "f60ab91b-7057-56fe-a4c0-17664472b776",
                    "quote": "According to popular legend, this textile tradition was started in the family of late Mohammad Siddiki when in the year 1586, Raja Bharmal I, invited his forefathers, to migrate from Sind and settle in Dhamadka, Kachchh.",
                    "locator": "§ \"Abstract\"",
                    "context": null,
                    "evidence": "QUOTED",
                    "level": "PROVISIONAL"
                  }
                ],
                "translated": false,
                "terms": []
              }
            },
            {
              "place": 2,
              "yearFrom": 2001,
              "yearTo": 2001,
              "sentence": {
                "id": "s4.b1.3",
                "text": "After a massive earthquake in 2001 the block printers were forced to relocate and settled in Ajrakhpur; over 100 families live there with 30 official workshops.",
                "level": "PROVISIONAL",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "id": "f3e38295-2a1b-5e12-8c1a-49897c72c260",
                    "claimId": "bc976cc1-204e-52e8-9b26-f1a91d33b7b3",
                    "sourceId": "d0f53ee9-4b97-5df7-a367-686957bdb7c8",
                    "quote": "After a massive earthquake in Kutch in 2001, the block printers were forced to relocate. They settled in Ajrakhpur village.",
                    "locator": "GI Journal No. 188 copy (application 1050), PDF p. 3",
                    "context": null,
                    "evidence": "QUOTED",
                    "level": "PROVISIONAL"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "9c5a26b8-9106-52eb-8704-2ebfd15db95a",
                    "claimId": "bc976cc1-204e-52e8-9b26-f1a91d33b7b3",
                    "sourceId": "d0f53ee9-4b97-5df7-a367-686957bdb7c8",
                    "quote": "There are over one hundred families living in Ajrakhpur, and 30 official block printing workshops; almost all of the families in Ajrakhpur generate their primary income from Ajrakh.",
                    "locator": "GI Journal No. 188 copy (application 1050), PDF p. 3",
                    "context": null,
                    "evidence": "QUOTED",
                    "level": "PROVISIONAL"
                  }
                ],
                "translated": false,
                "terms": []
              }
            }
          ],
