              "yearTo": 1631,
              "sentence": {
                "id": "s4.b1.4",
                "text": "Rao Bharmalji I (1586-1631) invited Khatri printers from Sindh and gave them land and tax exemptions.",
                "level": "PROVISIONAL",
                "citations": [
                  {
                    "id": "11b06c87-706e-57e1-9634-5fe424f7cd77",
                    "claimId": "66c8488c-11fe-5f1b-8653-dddbdaef2393",
                    "sourceId": "56c24809-a5fd-5d90-b6db-e55d7be09c07",
                    "quote": "The erstwhile ruler of Kutch Rao Bharmalji - I (1586-1631), invited the cloth-printing Khatri artisans from Sindh and gave them permission to settle and earn their livelihoods anywhere in Kutch. They were given land by the state as well spared any taxation on their produce.",
